      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the labeled maximum daily dose of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin in adults. The limit is lower for extended-release, which is 2,000 mg/day in the US. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThe dose may be a typo. Here are some options within the labeled limit:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the usual maximum for IR.\n- **1,700 mg PO total per day**, for example 850 mg twice daily with meals.\n- Another dose you choose that stays at or below 2,550 mg/day.\n\nTell me which dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. I can also add a note to the order if you'd like."
      }
