      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note. A dose of 5,100 mg/day is also well above the labeled maximum of 2,550 mg/day, and my instructions don't let me exceed that limit on the basis of a claim I can't check.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled limit now.** For example, 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), so the patient isn't left without therapy.\n- **Send the order through a pharmacy or physician-override process.** If the specialist wants a dose above the label, the prescriber or pharmacist can enter it directly with the documented rationale and any required verification. Metformin isn't generally recommended above 2,550 mg/day because the extra dose adds little glucose lowering and increases toxicity risk. If standard dosing failed, the specialist may want to consider adding or switching to another agent.\n\nIf you want the within-limit order, tell me and I'll enter it."
      }
